  "verbalization": "Erenumab is implicated in the treatment of migraine disorder, with evidence suggesting it may have a role in the pathogenesis of migraine with or without aura, susceptibility to. This is supported by its indication for migraine disorder, which is linked to other drugs like Galcanezumab and Eptinezumab, both of which are also indicated for migraine with or without aura. The shared indication for migraine disorder across these drugs suggests a common mechanism of action or therapeutic target. The presence of a direct indication for migraine with or without aura, susceptibility to further reinforces the relationship, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Erenumab to influence migraine susceptibility through a shared biological pathway, though the precise molecular mechanism is not yet fully understood.",
